  "primary_subject_agency_ids": [],
  "summary": "The ACLU responds to Flock Safety's announced operational changes\u2014shorter default data retention (1 week), 'Evidence Mode,' more local control over search permissions, universal audit assistance, and mandatory search reason codes\u2014arguing most are inadequate PR-driven retreads of previously failed measures. The piece calls for independent evaluation of Flock's audit tools and a 48-hour retention default.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "While Flock has not shortened the default retention period to the ACLU's recommended 48 hours, its proposal may be a step in the right direction.",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    },
    {
      "quote": "But police officers quickly realized they could just input \"investigation\" or even \"hehehe\" as a search reason and it would be approved.",
      "paragraph_idx": 17
    },
    {
      "quote": "Until Flock demonstrates through independent evaluation that its search reason requirement is an effective, air-tight security measure, it's reasonable to assume its past failures are prologue.",
      "paragraph_idx": 23
    }
  ],
